## RAG quickstart

This project includes optional RAG (retrieval-augmented generation) modules. Install RAG dependencies and use the CLI or API.

### Install RAG dependencies

```bash
uv sync --group rag
```

Use ModernBERT embeddings (optional):

```bash
uv sync --group rag --group rag-modernbert
```

### Choose embedding provider

By default, embeddings use sentence-transformers:

```bash
export RAG_EMBEDDER_PROVIDER=sentence_transformers
export RAG_EMBEDDER_MODEL=all-MiniLM-L6-v2
```

To use ModernBERT embeddings:

```bash
export RAG_EMBEDDER_PROVIDER=modernbert
export RAG_EMBEDDER_MODEL=answerdotai/ModernBERT-base
```

Reranking remains sentence-transformers based in this template.

### CLI

Ingest a document, then run a query:

```bash
{{ python_package_command_line_name }} rag ingest path/to/document.txt --corpus-id my_corpus
{{ python_package_command_line_name }} rag query "Your question here" --top-k 5
```

### API

{% if fastapi_enabled %}
Start the app and call the RAG endpoints:

```bash
# Health: which providers are configured
curl http://localhost:8000{{ fastapi_api_prefix }}/rag/health

# Query
curl -X POST http://localhost:8000{{ fastapi_api_prefix }}/rag/query \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"query": "Your question?", "top_k": 5}'

# Ingest (optional; can be disabled via config)
curl -X POST http://localhost:8000{{ fastapi_api_prefix }}/rag/ingest \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"path": "/path/to/file.txt", "corpus_id": "default"}'
```

Run the production-like container stack locally:

```bash
cp .env.prod.example .env.prod
$EDITOR .env.prod
make prod
```

`make prod` uses `docker compose up --build`, exposes the API on `http://localhost:8000`, and passes `OPENAI_API_KEY` into the container. Exporting `OPENAI_API_TOKEN` also works because the Make target normalizes it to `OPENAI_API_KEY` before Compose starts.
{% endif %}

